meta {
  name: Bulk Status
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

post {
  url: {{PRIVATE_BASE_URL}}/api/v1/admin/orders/bulk-status
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{ACCESS_TOKEN}}
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "status": "packed",
    "ids": ["{{ORDER_ID}}"]
  }
}

docs {
  # POST /api/v1/admin/orders/bulk-status

  Editor or superadmin. Up to 100 ids. Each order is checked on its own. The response is 200 even when some ids fail.

  ```json
  {
    "results": [
      { "id": "…", "ok": true, "status": "packed", "error": null },
      { "id": "…", "ok": false, "status": null, "error": "Cannot change an order from new to packed. Allowed: confirmed, cancelled" }
    ]
  }
  ```

  Allowed moves: new to confirmed or cancelled; confirmed to packed or cancelled; packed to shipped or cancelled; shipped to delivered or returned; delivered to returned. Cancelled and returned stop. Cancel puts the coupon use back and restores stock. Return restores stock and keeps the coupon use.
}
